WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-Welcome, everybody,
welcome, welcome,

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:04.470
welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.141
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.143
Well, let's get to some news.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:13.345
Guys, tomorrow, President Biden
and 40 other world leaders

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:16.749
are kicking off
a big virtual climate summit.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:19.452
Yep, they're meeting virtually
because of the pandemic.

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.054
Otherwise, they would have flown
40 different private jets

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:23.323
to a meeting about the climate.

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:24.924
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.194
Yep, the guest list includes
Vladimir Putin, Bill Gates,

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:31.964
Pope Francis, and one
very stressed out I.T. guy.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.466
[ Laughter ]
"Your Holiness,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.236
can you try closing the browser
and signing back in?"

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:37.871
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.006
It's too bad the summit
isn't in person.

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.541
If people were sitting
alphabetically,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:44.511
I'd love to hear the small talk
between the Pope and Putin.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:47.714
It's like,
"Do you watch 'Scheisse Creek'?

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.715
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.517
"Dan Levy is the best, I mean.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.752
Did you see episode
where Moira is --

00:00:53.752 --> 00:00:57.857
Oh, they're talking to us."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:00.626
That's right.
Vladimir Putin agreed to attend.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.061
It'll be weird
when someone says,

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.330
"Very funny torture rack
background, Vlad,"

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.233
and he's like,
"Right, joke, of course. Yes."

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.870
All I know is that it'll be
awkward when they start the Zoom

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.805
and Putin and Biden
are the first ones on.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.107
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.143
"Stop video. Stop.
Hi, Joe, how's it going, man?"

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.811
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:21.014
During the summit,
Biden is expected to announce

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.582
that the U.S. will cut
greenhouse gas emissions

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.219
at least in half by 2030.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:30.823
That's good. Yeah. Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.926
Yeah, Biden plans to cut
emissions by 2030, at which

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.095
point it will be President
Dwayne Johnson's problem.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.497
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:39.732
Hey, this is big.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.767
Remember that European soccer
Super League

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.436
that was just announced
two days ago?

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.371
-Yeah.
-Well, listen to this.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:48.274
-The proposed European
Super League may be over

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.276
before any teams
could even take the field.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.645
The league announced it was
suspending current plans

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.114
after the founding clubs
backed out of the venture

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.183
just two days
after the initial announcement.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.620
-Wow. Only two days.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.455
I've seen guacamole
last longer than that.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.956
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:07.460
Seriously, the leagued crumbled
faster than a Nature Valley bar.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.063
-Oy, oh, hey!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.998
-Yep, the Super League
has been knocked out,

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:15.735
and unlike most soccer injuries,
this one's real.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.336
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.906
Now those 12 teams are
showing up at their old leagues,

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.407
trying to act
like nothing happened.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.942
It's like, "Hey, what's up?

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.644
Does anyone here watch
'Shite's Creek'?"

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.911
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.047
"Dan Levy's fantastic.
He's brilliant. Yeah.

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:30.283
You see the episode
where Moira -- Oh, sorry."

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.785
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.855
Some business news --
Netflix stock took a big dive

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.023
this week after they reported

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:39.792
a dramatic slowdown
in subscriber growth.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.761
-Ooh!
-It's a tough time for Netflix.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.097
Right now, executives are
fighting like two people

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.932
looking for something
to watch on Netflix.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.299
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:49.535
Things are so bad,
the C.E.O. of Netflix was like,

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:52.171
"We either need a new
'Bridgerton' or a new pandemic."

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.506
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.775
But Netflix isn't letting
the news discourage them.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:59.611
They also announced that they're
spending more than $17 billion

00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:01.280
on content this year.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.250
Yeah, they're spending
$17 billion for shows

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.252
that we're just going to listen
to while we're on Instagram.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.820
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.290
Some more business news --
I saw that Lululemon is testing

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.828
a resale program where shoppers
sell and buy gently used items.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.363
-Ooh. Ooh.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.232
-Lululemon yoga pants.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.168
Let me put this in perspective.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:25.705
Wearing a pair of lightly used
Lululemon pants is basically

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.873
like picking up a pack of
lightly used Charmin.

00:03:27.873 --> 00:03:31.443
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:34.614
I don't even know how you'd sell
used Lululemons.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.050
Anybody who wears them has to
cut them off with scissors.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.350
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.685
I don't know.
Maybe this'll work.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:41.354
I mean, how many times have you
seen someone walking out

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.855
of a hot yoga class and thought,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.391
"I want those shorts,
that exact pair"?

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.959
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.327
Well, guys, you're not going to
believe this,

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.029
but the pandemic
has had an effect

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.331
on the sales of
Girl Scout cookies.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.699
Listen to this.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:56.936
-The lack of in-person sales
this year has left tons of

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.505
Thin Mints, Samoas,
and other flavors unsold.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.976
-Troop leaders in Atlanta say
they have 700,000 boxes

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.510
just sitting in a warehouse.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.811
-Wow.

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:07.347
I can't wait for my neighbor's
kid to be like,

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:09.014
"Oh, hi, Mr. Fallon,
so I can put you down

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:10.717
for 15,000 Do-Si-Dos?"

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.984
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:13.786
All I have to say is
you know America's broken

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.654
when there's a surplus
of delicious cookies

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.123
and life-saving vaccines.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.324
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.792
What are we doing?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:22.194
And get this -- in June,
New York City is getting

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:26.599
a 3-story, 21,000-square-foot
Harry Potter store.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.167
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.004
-It's exciting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.872
I'd say there's nothing hotter
right now than Harry Potter

00:04:33.872 --> 00:04:35.842
merchandise and indoor shopping,
would you agree?

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.478
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:41.813
It'll be the first time
a New Yorker can whip out

00:04:41.813 --> 00:04:44.016
their wand on the subway
without getting pepper-sprayed.

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.117
[ Laughter ]
What?

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.686
-Hey, hey!

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.821
Hey! Put away your Harry Potter.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:52.091
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.227
-I'm glad it's in New York City.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:55.995
What's better than hearing,
[Brooklyn accent] "Welcome to

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.830
the wizarding world
of Harry Potter"?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.132
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.600
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, the store is based on

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.135
the previously unreleased book,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:05.371
"Harry Potter and the Bunch Of
Stuff You Don't Need."

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.605
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:09.041
"Honey, let's stop in here.
Do we need a wand?

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.877
Oh, you answered
pretty quick there."

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.478
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:15.114
Well, there have been a lot of
incredible strides made

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.548
in science over the past year,

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.051
but here's an invention you
probably weren't expecting.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:19.918
Watch this.

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:21.954
-Engineers at Purdue University

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:24.990
have created
the whitest paint ever.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.394
They say the paint is so white
that coating a building with it

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.129
could cool them off enough

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:33.232
to reduce the need
for air-conditioning.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.700
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.869
Yeah, the "scientists" work at

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:39.305
the distinguished
University of Benjamin Moore.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.439
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.207
Can we see that paint color
again?

00:05:42.207 --> 00:05:43.476
Yeah, looks like a photo

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.444
from the Pillsbury Doughboy's
colonoscopy.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:48.280
[ Laughter ]
-Oh!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.218
-And finally, a Turkish musician
was scared to go paragliding

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.753
for the first time, so he
decided to bring something

00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.622
along to distract himself.
Check it out.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:06:06.198
♪♪

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:09.602
Yeah. What's weird is he also
overcomes his stage fright

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.371
by dressing like a skydiver.

